  "notes": "Forensic Molecular Biology option, University Park (of two options — the other, Forensic Chemistry, substitutes CHEM 227/FRNSC 425/427W for the BMB/FRNSC 420/421W sequence used here). Surfaced a real engine-level bug: BIOL 234/235W (lecture/lab) were scraped as BIDIRECTIONAL concurrent requirements (each needing the other same-term), which deadlocks the scheduler — neither can ever be picked, since evaluating either first finds the other not yet chosen. Fixed in biol_catalog.json the same way CHEM 110/111 already works: only the lab (235W) requires the lecture (234) concurrently, not the reverse. Also found and worked around a real prereq gap: the 'BIOL 222 or 322' requirement's own prerequisites (BIOL 110/141 or BMB 251/MICRB 201) are never otherwise part of this plan's own core sequence (FRNSC uses the BIOL 114/115/234/235W intro track instead) — modeled as a generic 'Genetics course' slot rather than guessing at an extra prerequisite course the sourced bulletin plan didn't call for; nothing downstream in this plan actually depends on BIOL 222/322 specifically (FRNSC 420's own prerequisite is independently satisfied via CHEM 212). The bulletin's suggested plan also lists 'FRNSC 415W' in both Third Year Spring and Fourth Year Fall, which is very likely a scrape duplication (the course isn't a 2-part sequence) — modeled once, in Third Year Spring, with a General Elective slot in its place the second time. 'etm' marks the gateway courses (Calc I, Chem I) everything downstream depends on.",
